The weather icon files in this directory (.svg, .png, .bin) are derived works
based on the Weather Icons project by Erik Flowers:

  https://github.com/erikflowers/weather-icons
  Copyright (C) 2014 Erik Flowers

The original icons are licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1.
The modified and converted versions in this directory are distributed under
the same license, as required by the OFL terms.

Modifications made for this project:
- Selected a subset of icons relevant to OpenWeatherMap condition categories,
  plus two non-weather glyphs (Thermometer, Raindrop) used for the indoor
  temperature/humidity readout on the dashboard's clock card
- Redrawn / adjusted SVG paths to fit a 64×64 pixel grid for e-Paper display
  (weather condition icons only; Thermometer.svg / Raindrop.svg are used
  unmodified from the upstream wi-thermometer.svg / wi-raindrop.svg,
  30×30 viewBox as in the original)
- Exported SVG → PNG via Inkscape (assets/weather_icons/convert.bat) for the
  weather condition icons; Thermometer.svg and Raindrop.svg were exported to
  PNG via resvg (https://github.com/linebender/resvg) instead, same source
  format and output size, tool substitution only
- PNG files are loaded at runtime by Pillow and resized on-the-fly for rendering
  on the Waveshare 7.3" e-Paper (epd7in3e) display
- Thermometer.png and Raindrop.png are loaded as alpha masks (not pasted as-is)
  so the glyph can be tinted at runtime — see _load_mono_icon_mask() in
  app/display/renderer_utils.py

The icons in this directory use the name "epaper-weather-icons" to distinguish
them from the original Weather Icons set, in accordance with OFL section 3.

